---
title: Why "AI-Assisted" is the only honest way to build in 2026.
publishedAt: '2026-04-10'
pillar: tech-ai
summary: >-
  Stop pretending you aren't using LLMs. Here is how I use them to build sites
  faster and more accurately than a manual developer.
---
There is a profound vanity in the tech sector right now: developers pretending they write every line of code by hand. Let’s abandon that. 

Using an LLM isn't cheating; it’s an operational moat. If I can architect a full Next.js stack with semantic routing, design system integration, and CMS wiring in a fraction of the time a manual developer takes, the client wins. The value is in the system logic, the conversion capacity, and the strategic positioning—not the manual keystrokes.
